<title>INDIA: India Tata Tea 96/97 1 half net up 25 pct.</title>
<headline>India Tata Tea 96/97 1 half net up 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	353.0    vs     283.1</p>
<p>    Income from</p>
<p>    operations    3,146.7    vs   2,244.5</p>
<p>    Other income    107.8    vs     113.0</p>
<p>    Total income  3,254.5    vs   2,357.5</p>
<p>    Expenditure   2,522.9    vs   1,822.3</p>
<p>    Interest (net)  137.0    vs	61.4</p>
<p>    Gross profit    594.6    vs     473.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation     54.9    vs	48.3</p>
<p>    Taxation	  186.7    vs     142.4</p>
<p>Note:India's largest tea firm Tata Tea Ltd said turnover on its core operations rose by 21 percent over last year. Export turnover was up 70 percent at 1.05 billion rupees. Tata Tea said figures for the year-ago period have been adjusted for impact of increased wages in Kerala.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
